---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
---
<Base title="Tracebook — AI tech support for machine OEMs">
<!-- ─── HERO ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="relative overflow-hidden">
  <div class="mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-10 px-6 py-16 md:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12 lg:gap-14">
    <div class="lg:col-span-5">
      <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">
        ⌖ tracebook support · for machinery builders
      </div>

      <h1 class="mt-6 font-display text-5xl font-medium leading-[0.98] tracking-tight text-ink md:text-6xl">
        The 2 a.m. call <em class="italic wonk">answers itself.</em>
      </h1>

      <div class="mt-8 hairline-gold w-40"></div>

      <p class="mt-8 max-w-xl font-display italic text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft md:text-xl"
         style="font-variation-settings: '&quot;opsz&quot; 24, &quot;SOFT&quot; 100, &quot;WONK&quot; 0;">
        Tracebook turns your shelf of PDFs, your YouTube backlog, and
        your resolved-ticket history into a sourced, cited AI tech
        support agent — running under your brand.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-4">
        <a href="mailto:cmisztur@mriiot.com?subject=Tracebook%20demo"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-ink px-5 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-paper hover:bg-inkSoft">
          Book a demo
          <span class="font-mono text-xs">→</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#how"
           class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-medium text-ink underline decoration-gold decoration-2 underline-offset-4 hover:text-inkSoft">
          See how it works
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex items-center gap-3 text-xs text-inkMute">
        <span class="font-mono uppercase tracking-eyebrow">live customer</span>
        <span class="font-display italic text-inkSoft">Royal Master Grinders</span>
      </div>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-md text-xs text-inkMute italic">
        Watch a real diagnostic session resolve →
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Animated chat replay -->
    <div class="lg:col-span-7">
      <div id="chat-demo" class="relative">
        <div class="absolute -left-3 top-3 -z-10 h-full w-full rounded-md bg-gold/15"></div>
        <article class="overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-ink/30 bg-paper shadow-[0_2px_24px_rgba(26,26,26,0.08)]">
          <!-- Header strip mimics customer-portal session header -->
          <header class="flex items-center justify-between border-b border-ink/15 bg-paperDeep/50 px-5 py-3">
            <div class="flex items-baseline gap-3">
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">support session</span>
              <span class="font-mono text-xs text-ink" id="chat-machine">Generation X · #SN-3648</span>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
              <span class="inline-block h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-visual"></span>
              <span class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-inkMute">live</span>
            </div>
          </header>

          <div id="chat-body" class="space-y-4 px-5 py-5 h-[520px] overflow-y-auto"></div>

          <footer class="flex items-center justify-between border-t border-ink/15 bg-paperDeep/50 px-5 py-3">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-inkMute">
              <span id="chat-status">tracebook.support · acme manufacturing</span>
            </div>
            <button id="chat-replay"
                    class="hidden font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-ink hover:text-gold">
              ↻ replay
            </button>
          </footer>
        </article>
        <div class="mt-3 text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-inkMute">
          <span class="font-mono">a real diagnostic, replayed</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── LIVE DEMO WIDGET ───────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="border-t border-ink/10 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6">
    <h2 class="text-center font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
      Try it, <em class="italic wonk">right here</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-xl text-center font-display italic text-lg text-inkSoft">
      This is the exact experience your customers would get — pointed at
      a demo equipment library instead of yours.
    </p>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-4 max-w-2xl text-center text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
      Below is one live machine — serial 3516, a TG-12 precision grinder —
      with its real manuals, electrical drawings, and parts lists indexed.
      Ask anything a service tech would (or tap an example question); the
      answer streams back citing the exact pages and drawings it came
      from. No login, no signup.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 rounded-lg border border-ink/15 bg-paper p-8"
         data-tracebook-demo="support"
         data-api="https://support.demo.tracebook.ai"
         data-questions='["What color are the wires between the linear drive and the motor?","What is the bill of materials for the SA-4071 assembly?","List all the circuit breakers on this machine as a table","My linear drive is not working. How do I diagnose the fault, and what do the status indicators / error codes on the drive mean?"]'>
      <div class="text-center">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">live demo</div>
        <div class="mt-4 inline-flex items-center gap-3 rounded-md border border-ink/15 bg-paperDeep/60 px-5 py-3 text-sm text-inkMute">
          coming online
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ─── PROBLEM ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="problem" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-paperDeep/40 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
      The same questions, <em class="italic wonk">again and again.</em>
    </h2>
    <div class="mt-12 grid gap-10 md:grid-cols-3">
      <article class="border-t-2 border-dense pt-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-dense">it's 2 a.m.</div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl leading-snug">The customer wants help.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Your service manager is asleep. The right answer is in a
          400-page manual nobody else on the team has read cover-to-cover.
          The customer ends up off-spec or off-line until morning.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="border-t-2 border-dense pt-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-dense">scattered</div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl leading-snug">Your knowledge is in eight places.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Manuals in Dropbox, drawings on a shared drive, training videos
          on YouTube, the <em>real</em> answers in a five-year-old email
          thread. Even your senior tech can&rsquo;t find the one PDF where
          it&rsquo;s documented.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article class="border-t-2 border-dense pt-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-dense">looped</div>
        <p class="mt-3 font-display text-2xl leading-snug">Same fix, twelve times a year.</p>
        <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          &ldquo;Linear motor not moving&rdquo; comes in twelve times a
          year. The fix is always the cable transport module. Nobody
          wrote it down where the next customer would find it.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── HOW IT WORKS ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="how" class="border-t border-ink/10 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
      Three steps. <em class="italic wonk">No magic.</em>
    </h2>

    <ol class="mt-14 space-y-12">
      <li class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-2">
          <div class="font-display text-7xl font-medium text-gold leading-none">①</div>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-10">
          <h3 class="font-display text-3xl font-medium">Upload what you&rsquo;ve got.</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
            PDFs of operating manuals, electrical schematics, mechanical
            drawings. YouTube links. Photos of HMI screens. Resolved
            ticket threads from past support work. Tracebook indexes all
            of it &mdash; per machine model, per customer.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-2">
          <div class="font-display text-7xl font-medium text-gold leading-none">②</div>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-10">
          <h3 class="font-display text-3xl font-medium">Your customer asks a question.</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
            Typed, or as a phone photo of a fault screen, or as a
            30-second video clip of the noise the machine is making. The
            system reads it, retrieves the relevant pages of the
            relevant documents, and answers.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>

      <li class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-12">
        <div class="md:col-span-2">
          <div class="font-display text-7xl font-medium text-gold leading-none">③</div>
        </div>
        <div class="md:col-span-10">
          <h3 class="font-display text-3xl font-medium">Every claim is cited.</h3>
          <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
            The answer points back to the exact page of the exact
            document. If the AI doesn&rsquo;t know, the chat escalates
            into a ticket routed to your team. Every resolved ticket
            becomes a new entry in the knowledge base, so the next
            customer with the same question doesn&rsquo;t have to wait.
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── FEATURE GRID ───────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="features" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-paperDeep/40 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
      Built for the way you actually <em class="italic wonk">support customers.</em>
    </h2>

    <div class="mt-14 grid gap-px overflow-hidden rounded-md border border-ink/15 bg-ink/15 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <!-- 6 feature tiles separated by 1px ink hairlines via gap trick -->
      <div class="bg-paper p-7">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">grounded</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-medium">Cited answers, not guesses.</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Every claim links back to the exact page of the source
          document. Open the citation; the customer can verify for
          themselves.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-7">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">scoped</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-medium">Per-machine knowledge base.</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          A customer asking about <em>their</em> serial number sees
          their machine&rsquo;s docs first &mdash; including private
          quotes, sales orders, and customer-specific drawings.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-7">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">white-label</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-medium">Your brand, your domain.</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          The customer-facing portal carries your logo, your colors,
          and lives at <span class="font-mono">support.yourcompany.com</span>.
          Tracebook is invisible.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-7">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">multi-modal</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-medium">Photos and video clips.</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          The customer attaches a phone shot of a fault screen or a
          30-second video of the machine sound. The system describes
          it and uses the description to search.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-7">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">closed loop</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-medium">Tickets feed the loop.</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Unresolved chats become tickets your technicians work on.
          When the ticket resolves, the fix becomes a new entry in
          the knowledge base &mdash; automatically.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-paper p-7">
        <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">isolated</div>
        <h3 class="mt-2 font-display text-xl font-medium">Single-tenant, your data.</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Each OEM is a separately deployed instance on Google Cloud.
          Your data does not cross tenant boundaries. Nothing trains
          third-party models.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── LIVE CUSTOMER ──────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="border-t border-ink/10 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6">
    <div class="grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <h2 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
          Live with a <em class="italic wonk">real OEM,</em> right now.
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Royal Master Grinders &mdash; a precision-grinder OEM with a
          fleet of machines deployed across North America &mdash; runs
          their entire customer support flow on Tracebook. Manuals,
          drawings, training videos, and historical case files were
          ingested in two weeks. Their service team has been answering
          fewer 2 a.m. calls ever since.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-6 max-w-xl font-display italic text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          &ldquo;That&rsquo;s exactly what I wanted to see. It&rsquo;s
          just putting the pieces together &mdash; wow.&rdquo;
          <span class="block mt-2 not-italic font-body text-sm text-inkMute">
            &mdash; John, Royal Master Grinders, watching the system
            diagnose a real Gen-X fault.
          </span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="border border-ink/30 bg-paper p-8 shadow-[0_2px_24px_rgba(26,26,26,0.06)]">
          <div class="font-mono text-[10px] uppercase tracking-eyebrow text-gold">at-a-glance</div>
          <dl class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm">
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-ink/15 pb-2">
              <dt class="text-inkSoft">Machine fleet indexed</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-base font-bold">200 machines</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-ink/15 pb-2">
              <dt class="text-inkSoft">Manuals + drawings</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-base font-bold">2,000+ docs</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between border-b border-ink/15 pb-2">
              <dt class="text-inkSoft">Customer chat sessions</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-base font-bold">live</dd>
            </div>
            <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between">
              <dt class="text-inkSoft">Time to first answer</dt>
              <dd class="font-mono text-base font-bold">&lt; 30s typical</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── PRICING ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="border-t border-ink/10 py-20">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 text-center">
    <h2 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
      Per-OEM SaaS. <em class="italic wonk">Quote-based.</em>
    </h2>
    <p class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
      Pricing scales with your machine fleet and document volume.
      Smaller OEMs land lower than you&rsquo;d expect; bigger fleets
      get bulk-tier rates. Reach out for a quote &mdash; we&rsquo;ll
      ballpark in 24 hours.
    </p>
    <a href="mailto:cmisztur@mriiot.com?subject=Tracebook%20pricing"
       class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-ink px-6 py-3 text-sm font-medium text-paper hover:bg-inkSoft">
      Get a quote
      <span class="font-mono text-xs">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── FAQ ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section id="faq" class="border-t border-ink/10 bg-paperDeep/40 py-24">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6">
    <h2 class="font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-5xl">
      The <em class="italic wonk">real</em> questions.
    </h2>

    <dl class="mt-12 divide-y divide-ink/15 border-t border-ink/15">
      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">Where does my data live?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          In your dedicated tenant on Google Cloud. Each OEM is a
          separately deployed instance with its own database, file
          storage, and vector index. Your data does not cross tenant
          boundaries.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">What happens if the AI doesn't know the answer?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          The chat escalates into a ticket. A real technician on your
          team takes over; the customer can attach files; the conversation
          continues until resolved. The resolved ticket becomes structured
          knowledge the next chat can retrieve from.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">Do you train on my data?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          No. Your data is not used to train any third-party model.
          Inference happens on Google Vertex AI; retrieval happens
          against your tenant&rsquo;s own vector index.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">How long does setup take?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Two weeks for a typical OEM with ~10 machine models and a
          few hundred documents. The bulk of that time is uploading
          and tagging content &mdash; we run alongside you on it.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">What machines / industries does this work for?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Anything where the customer is supported via written manuals,
          schematics, and historical knowledge: precision tools,
          packaging machines, food-and-beverage equipment, building
          systems. The first deployed customer is in machine-tool
          grinding; the same plumbing applies to any OEM with shipped
          machines under warranty.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">Can I use my own logo and domain?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Yes. The customer-facing portal lives at your subdomain
          (<span class="font-mono">support.yourcompany.com</span> for
          example) with your logo and brand colors. Tracebook does
          not appear in the customer experience.
        </p>
      </details>

      <details class="group py-6">
        <summary class="flex cursor-pointer items-baseline justify-between gap-4 text-lg">
          <span class="font-display text-xl">What does it cost?</span>
          <span class="font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:hidden">+</span>
          <span class="hidden font-mono text-sm text-inkMute group-open:inline">−</span>
        </summary>
        <p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl text-base leading-relaxed text-inkSoft">
          Per-OEM SaaS, scaled by fleet size and document volume.
          Email <a href="mailto:cmisztur@mriiot.com" class="text-ink underline decoration-gold underline-offset-2">cmisztur@mriiot.com</a>
          for a 24-hour ballpark.
        </p>
      </details>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- ─── CTA ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
<section class="border-t border-ink/10 py-28">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 text-center">
    <h2 class="font-display text-5xl font-medium leading-tight md:text-6xl">
      Want to see it on
      <em class="italic wonk">your</em> data?
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-inkSoft">
      A 30-minute demo, plus a per-OEM ballpark within 24 hours.
    </p>
    <a href="mailto:cmisztur@mriiot.com?subject=Tracebook%20demo"
       class="mt-10 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-ink px-7 py-4 text-base font-medium text-paper hover:bg-inkSoft">
      Email cmisztur@mriiot.com
      <span class="font-mono text-sm">→</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>


<!-- Demo transcript — inlined so the page works via file:// (browsers
     block fetch on file:// for security, which would otherwise leave
     the chat empty when previewing without a local server). To edit,
     change this block; the sibling assets/demo-conversation.json is
     kept for reference and documentation only. -->
<script id="chat-transcript" type="application/json">
{
  "machine": {
    "model": "Generation X",
    "serial": "SN-3648",
    "customer": "Acme Manufacturing"
  },
  "turns": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "delay_ms": 800,
      "text": "Linear motor not moving."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "delay_ms": 1200,
      "thinking_ms": 2200,
      "text": "Linear-motor-not-moving is a common Gen X fault. Before we go into the drive electronics, let's rule out the basics:\n\n1. **Mechanical freedom** — does the carriage move freely by hand with the drive disabled?\n2. **Drive fault LEDs** — any red indicators on the Compax3 panel?\n3. **Limit switches** — are both end-of-travel switches reading their normal state?\n\nIf all three are clean, we'll go to the error history next.",
      "citations": [
        { "n": 1, "type": "manual", "title": "Compax3 Service Manual", "page": "p178" },
        { "n": 2, "type": "historical_case", "title": "Linear motor — initial checklist" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "delay_ms": 1500,
      "text": "Mechanical is fine, no fault LEDs, limit switches green. Resistance across phases is fine but no encoder counts. Read head and tape look clean."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "delay_ms": 1100,
      "thinking_ms": 2600,
      "text": "Encoder reading clean but no counts on the drive — that's a **feedback-level-low** error pattern, not a phase or motor problem. There's a Royal Master historical case where this exact symptom on a Gen X was traced back to **flex fatigue in the cable transport module**.",
      "citations": [
        { "n": 3, "type": "historical_case", "title": "Feedback level low — cable transport flex fatigue" },
        { "n": 4, "type": "drawing", "title": "Cable Transport Module — Gen X", "page": "p4" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "user",
      "delay_ms": 1500,
      "text": "Could it be the cable transport module?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "delay_ms": 900,
      "thinking_ms": 2400,
      "text": "**Primary suspect.** The historical case matches your symptoms exactly: feedback-level-low on the drive, encoder hardware testing clean, no fault LEDs upstream. The flex cables inside the transport module fatigue over machine-cycles and intermittently lose continuity — the encoder sees signal but the drive doesn't see counts. There's a YouTube walkthrough for the replacement.",
      "citations": [
        { "n": 3, "type": "historical_case", "title": "Feedback level low — cable transport flex fatigue" },
        { "n": 5, "type": "youtube", "title": "Cable transport module replacement — Gen X" },
        { "n": 6, "type": "manual", "title": "Compax3 Service Manual", "page": "p214" }
